{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/netzeroexpeditions/items/518959/", "pk": 518959, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/netzeroexpeditions/", "pk": 62352, "shortname": "netzeroexpeditions", "name": "Net Zero Expeditions", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "Blue Whale Expedition", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 8, "unicode": "Blue Whale Expedition", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": false, "sold_out_text": "", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 2.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_reached_hours": 1.0, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 1, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 250, "description": "# Full Day Blue Whale Experience!\n\n## Duration\n4 to 6 Hours\n\n#### Note: If three or less passengers book this expedition the duration will be limited to four hours. \n\n## Rates\n$299 per person. \n\n#### Plus taxes and booking fees\n#### We need a minimum of two people to run this trip, if you are a single passenger and no one has booked the day you wan to go please call us to make arrangements.\n\n## About\nEvery summer the mythical Blue Whale visits the nutrient rich waters off San Diego. Join us on a long range whale watch expedition for a fantastic encounter with one of the most iconic of all the great whales. We run our  Blue whale expeditions in June and July at the peak of the Blue Whale Season.\n\nThe length of the expedition ranges from four to eight hours providing with enough time to cover a wide area of ocean opening the opportunity to encounter Blue Whales, Fin Whales, Offshore Bottlenose Dolphins, Common Dolphins, Sea lions, amongst other marine mammals.  \n\nOn this thrilling wildlife tour we'll explore up to 100 miles off San Diego's Offshore waters specifically in search for Blue Whales and other exotic whale species. Our Blue Whale private expedition departs from mission bay in San Diego at a custom time determined by the weather forecast and our guests preferences.\n\n## More Info\n- **Availability:** End of May-  August\n- **Location of Departure/Return:** Mission bay, San Diego California. \n- **Gratuities:** Although never expected, gratuities are a great way of saying thanks to our hard-working crew. \n- **Max capacity:** 6 Guests per boat\nWe can accommodate for groups of maximum 12 people in two boats.\n- Please note our Zodiac boat cruises at 20+ mph and although our Captain will maneuver to avoid 'bumps' there's always the possibility to encounter unexpected rough seas. With this in mind, we do not recommend our expeditions for people with back or neck problems.", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "Mission Bay, San Diego CA", "booking_notes": "### Boarding Instructions:\nPlease arrive 15 minutes prior to your boarding time and make sure to fill out your waivers electronically.\n\n## What to Bring\n- We suggest you bring a reusable bottle of water lunch and/or snacks.\n- It’s always a great idea to bring warm clothing, a sweater and a rain jacket (Layering works wonders) We'll also be under the sun so please bring biodegradable sunscreen, sunglasses and a hat.\n- Our Zodiac boat has a low center of gravity minimizing rocking motion. However, If prone to seasickness we recommend you to take the seasickness medicine the night before your expedition and another dose 30 minutes before the trip.", "cancellation